# Cross-platform parity (Chrome, Mac, Windows)

Rewrite Better ships the **same writing panel** on three platforms. Any product change in the app must land on **all three** in the same change:

| Platform | Root |
|----------|------|
| Chrome extension | `chrome/` |
| macOS (SwiftUI) | `mac/` |
| Windows (Tauri) | `win/` |

Do not finish a feature, bugfix, copy, prompt, option, or UI change on only one platform.

## Shared logic map

Port the same behavior. Chrome `shared/` and Windows `ui/` are JS; Mac is Swift.

| Concern | Chrome | Windows | macOS |
|---------|--------|---------|-------|
| Panel UI / flow | `chrome/shared/panel.js` | `win/ui/panel.js` | `Views/PanelView.swift`, `Services/PanelController.swift` |
| Prompts | `chrome/shared/prompts.js` | `win/ui/prompts.js` | `Services/PromptBuilder.swift`, `WritingAssistPrompts.swift` |
| Options / tones / formats | `chrome/shared/options.js` | `win/ui/options.js` | `Models/Options.swift` |
| i18n (EN / VI) | `chrome/shared/i18n.js` | `win/ui/i18n.js` | `Models/L10n.swift` |
| LLM providers / failover | `chrome/shared/llm-providers.js` | `win/ui/llm-providers.js` | `Services/LLMProviders.swift` |
| Diff | `chrome/shared/diff.js` | `win/ui/diff.js` | `Services/ResultDiff.swift` |
| Writing assist | `chrome/shared/writing-assist.js` | `win/ui/writing-assist.js` | `WritingAssistController.swift` |
| Daily key skip | `chrome/shared/daily-skip.js` | `win/ui/daily-skip.js` | `Services/DailyKeySkipStore.swift` |
| Settings UI | `chrome/options.html`, `options.js` | `win/ui/settings.html`, `settings.js` | `Views/SettingsView.swift` |
| Styles (Chrome / Win) | `chrome/styles.css` | `win/ui/styles.css` | SwiftUI views |

If you add a string, option, prompt, or panel control, add it in **all three** columns.

## Platform-only (do not copy blindly)

Keep native where the OS requires it. Still document the equivalent if the **user-visible** behavior should match.

- **Chrome only:** `manifest.json`, content/popup shells, `chrome.storage`, context menu, in-page replace
- **macOS only:** Accessibility capture, Keychain, menu bar, Carbon hotkey, paste-back
- **Windows only:** Tauri tray/hotkey, `win/src-tauri/`, local key storage, paste-back

`web/` is the marketing site, not a fourth app. Update it only when downloads, screenshots, or public copy must match the product.

## Done when

1. Behavior, copy, prompts, and settings match on Chrome, Mac, and Windows (except true OS constraints).
2. Tests for that logic are updated on each platform that has them (`chrome/shared/*.test.js`, `win/ui/*.test.js`, `mac/.../RewriteBetterTests`).
3. The change is not left as a TODO on another platform.

```text
❌ BAD: add a rewrite tone in chrome/shared/options.js and ship
✅ GOOD: same tone in chrome/shared/options.js, win/ui/options.js, and mac Options.swift (plus i18n / L10n)
```
